{% if analysis.publish_dir or analysis.build_command %}
     At the END of the Build job, publish the compiled build output artifact using
     `PublishPipelineArtifact@1` (targetPath: '$(Build.SourcesDirectory)/{% if analysis.working_dir %}{{ analysis.working_dir }}/{% endif %}{{ analysis.publish_dir or "dist" }}', artifact: 'drop', publishLocation: 'pipeline'). NEVER publish the workspace root (`$(Build.SourcesDirectory)` or `.`).
{% endif %}
  2. A "Test" job (dependsOn: Build) containing the applicable setup, cache, install, test, and publish steps listed below.
{% if analysis.publish_dir or analysis.build_command %}
     At the START of the Test job (after setup/cache/install), download the build artifact using
     `DownloadPipelineArtifact@2` (buildType: 'current', artifact: 'drop', targetPath: '$(Build.SourcesDirectory)/{% if analysis.working_dir %}{{ analysis.working_dir }}/{% endif %}{{ analysis.publish_dir or "dist" }}')
     BEFORE running any test command. Only use `--no-build` or equivalent skip-build flags when
     this download step is present in the same job.
  IMPORTANT: Jobs in Azure Pipelines do NOT share a filesystem. The Build job MUST publish its
